From: Neutron lab (fg187) 
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: a WS_EX_NOACTIVATE top-level activated implicitly never takes the foreground from another thread

What he saw (Illustrator 2026, runtime 186): "ctrl q did not work after clicking on those panels. It only worked after I
clicked somewhere else" / "There was nothing "in front" I used a mouse and there was no dialog. It was a simple new and
blank document."

Mechanism (his log illustrator-adobe2026-20261110-125005.log, WINEDEBUG=+key,+win, SOLID): Illustrator's AGM graphics
thread owns a never-shown top-level "AGM Invisible Window" (ex 08000000 WS_EX_NOACTIVATE, style 06000000) and resizes it
with SetWindowPos(NOMOVE|NOZORDER|NOREDRAW) -- no SWP_NOACTIVATE -- whenever the canvas changes; once, at creation, it
also calls SetFocus on it. set_window_pos() always ended in set_foreground_window() without SWP_NOACTIVATE, and
NtUserSetFocus() goes through set_foreground_window() when the calling thread has nothing active. Every foreground move
by that thread in his log (6, the failing one right after his click on a panel made the main window foreground) sits
inside such a SetWindowPos. The hidden window became the foreground window, his Ctrl+Q went to the AGM thread's queue,
which ignores keys, and only a click on the canvas (main window foreground again) made the next Ctrl+Q work.

Windows (fgsteal.exe reference probe, his PC, Win11 26200, 11-10): the same SetWindowPos on a hidden or visible
WS_EX_NOACTIVATE window, and SetFocus on it, activate the window FOR ITS OWN THREAD only -- it gets WM_ACTIVATEAPP 1,
WM_NCACTIVATE 0, WM_ACTIVATE, WM_SETFOCUS and its thread's active = focus = it -- while the foreground window, its
activation and the keyboard stay with the main window (no deactivation messages there). An explicit
SetForegroundWindow from the same process still moves the foreground (measured, arm d) and is not touched.

Fix: neutron_noactivate_keepfg() (input.c) -- for a non-child top-level with WS_EX_NOACTIVATE, owned by the calling
thread, while the foreground window belongs to another thread, set_window_pos's implicit activation and SetFocus's
no-active-window activation call set_active_window() for this thread instead of set_foreground_window(). WM_NCACTIVATE
goes out as 0 there because the window is not the foreground window, as on Windows. When the caller holds the
foreground, or nothing is foreground, the upstream path runs unchanged.
Also: set_active_window() returned its `ret` uninitialized when the window was already active (gcc's
-Wmaybe-uninitialized at that line); with background activation that case is now common (SetForegroundWindow on a
window its thread already has active returned garbage in the lab, e.g. -1356560, 7 -- also seen once on 186). It now
returns TRUE there: nothing to do is success.

Not covered (Wine still differs from his Windows run, left for later):
- a window WITHOUT the flag (probe arm b): Windows' foreground lock keeps a later implicit SetWindowPos activation in
  the background once the user has given input elsewhere; Wine still moves the foreground there.
- a second process (arm e): Windows refuses its SetForegroundWindow after the user's input in the first process
  (returns 0); Wine allows it for a child of the foreground process (server/queue.c is_current_process_foreground).

Lab evidence (runtime 11.10-186fg = 186 + this win32u.so only; desk f7a, scratch prefix, fgsteal.exe):
- 186fg 2/2: arms a/c/d/f print his Windows lines (a: after 1st SetWindowPos fg=M, M active/focus=M, T2 active/focus=W,
  W gets WM_ACTIVATEAPP 1 / WM_NCACTIVATE 0 / WM_ACTIVATE / WM_SETFOCUS, F13 -> M; c the same visible; d F13 -> T2;
  f F13 -> M); 5 neutron-noactivate-keepfg lines per run.
- kill switch NEUTRON_NOACTIVATE_SWP_KEEPFG=0 on the same build 2/2 = 186 (3/3): every arm F13 -> T2.
- Wine user32 conformance tests win/msg/input (standalone build from this tree): see NOTES (186 vs 186fg).

Kill switch: NEUTRON_NOACTIVATE_SWP_KEEPFG=0. Diagnostic: NEUTRON_WL_DIAG=1 prints one neutron-noactivate-keepfg line
per background activation, after it happened.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -2018,6 +2018,8 @@
     if (previous == hwnd)
     {
         if (prev) *prev = hwnd;
+        ret = TRUE;  /* NEUTRON noactivate-keepfg: nothing to do is success; ret was returned uninitialized here, so
+                      * SetForegroundWindow() on a window already active for its (background) thread returned garbage */
         goto done;
     }
 
@@ -2270,6 +2272,64 @@
     return on;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON noactivate-keepfg (2026-11-10): the implicit activation of a WS_EX_NOACTIVATE top-level never moves the
+ * foreground away from another thread.
+ *
+ * Illustrator 2026: "ctrl q did not work after clicking on those panels. It only worked after I clicked somewhere
+ * else". Illustrator's AGM graphics thread owns a never-shown top-level "AGM Invisible Window" (ex 08000000
+ * WS_EX_NOACTIVATE, style 06000000) and resizes it with SetWindowPos(NOMOVE|NOZORDER|NOREDRAW), without
+ * SWP_NOACTIVATE, whenever the canvas changes; it also calls SetFocus on it once. set_window_pos() and
+ * NtUserSetFocus() (when the calling thread has nothing active) reached set_foreground_window(), so the hidden
+ * window became the foreground window and every key went to the AGM thread's queue, which ignores them
+ * (illustrator-adobe2026-20261110-125005.log: 0ab4 set_foreground_window 0x20b86 right after its SetWindowPos,
+ * previous = the main window 0x1006c the user had just clicked).
+ *
+ * Windows (fgsteal probe, Win11 26200, his PC, 11-10): the same SetWindowPos -- hidden or visible window -- and
+ * SetFocus activate the window FOR ITS OWN THREAD only (WM_ACTIVATEAPP 1, WM_NCACTIVATE 0, WM_ACTIVATE,
+ * WM_SETFOCUS; GetGUIThreadInfo active = focus = it), the foreground window, its activation and the keyboard stay
+ * where they were. An explicit SetForegroundWindow from the same process still moves the foreground (also
+ * measured) and is not touched here.
+ *
+ * Only these two implicit paths, only for a non-child top-level with WS_EX_NOACTIVATE owned by the calling thread,
+ * and only while the foreground window belongs to another thread: the window is activated in the background with
+ * set_active_window() (WM_NCACTIVATE goes out as 0 because it is not the foreground window). When the caller
+ * already holds the foreground, or nothing is foreground, the upstream path runs unchanged.
+ * Not covered: Windows' foreground lock for a window WITHOUT the flag (a later implicit activation after user
+ * input elsewhere stays in the background there too; Wine still moves the foreground), and a second process's
+ * SetForegroundWindow after the user's input (refused on Windows, allowed here for a child of the foreground
+ * process).
+ *
+ * Kill switch NEUTRON_NOACTIVATE_SWP_KEEPFG=0 restores the upstream behaviour; NEUTRON_WL_DIAG=1 prints one
+ * neutron-noactivate-keepfg line per background activation, after it happened. */
+BOOL neutron_noactivate_keepfg( HWND top, const char *caller, BOOL *ok )
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    DWORD tid = GetCurrentThreadId(), fg_tid;
+    HWND fg;
+
+    if (!top || (get_window_long( top, GWL_STYLE ) & (WS_POPUP | WS_CHILD)) == WS_CHILD) return FALSE;
+    if (!(get_window_long( top, GWL_EXSTYLE ) & WS_EX_NOACTIVATE)) return FALSE;
+    if (get_window_thread( top, NULL ) != tid) return FALSE;
+    if (!(fg = NtUserGetForegroundWindow()) || fg == top) return FALSE;
+    if ((fg_tid = get_window_thread( fg, NULL )) == tid || !fg_tid) return FALSE;
+    if (on < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_NOACTIVATE_SWP_KEEPFG" );
+        on = e ? (e[0] != '0') : 1;
+        ERR( "neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_NOACTIVATE_SWP_KEEPFG = %d (%s)\n", on, e ? "environment" : "default" );
+    }
+    if (!on) return FALSE;
+
+    *ok = TRUE;
+    if (get_active_window() == top) return TRUE;   /* already active for this thread: nothing changes */
+    *ok = set_active_window( top, NULL, FALSE, TRUE, 0 );
+    if (neutron_wl_diag())
+        ERR( "neutron-noactivate-keepfg: %s(%p) exstyle %08x -> activated for its thread %04x only (ret %d, active now %p), foreground stays %p (thread %04x)\n",
+             caller, top, (unsigned int)get_window_long( top, GWL_EXSTYLE ), (unsigned int)tid, *ok,
+             get_active_window(), NtUserGetForegroundWindow(), (unsigned int)fg_tid );
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
 /**********************************************************************
  *           NtUserSetActiveWindow    (win32u.@)
  */
@@ -2495,7 +2555,17 @@
         if (call_hooks( WH_CBT, HCBT_SETFOCUS, (WPARAM)hwnd, (LPARAM)previous, 0 )) return 0;
 
         /* activate hwndTop if needed. */
-        if (!(active = get_active_window()) && !set_foreground_window( hwndTop, FALSE, FALSE )) return 0;
+        if (!(active = get_active_window()))
+        {
+            BOOL ok;
+
+            /* NEUTRON noactivate-keepfg: a WS_EX_NOACTIVATE top-level is activated for this thread only */
+            if (neutron_noactivate_keepfg( hwndTop, "SetFocus", &ok ))
+            {
+                if (!ok) return 0;
+            }
+            else if (!set_foreground_window( hwndTop, FALSE, FALSE )) return 0;
+        }
         if (hwndTop != active)
         {
             if (neutron_noactivate_refuse( hwndTop, active ))
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -5314,7 +5314,14 @@
         if ((style & (WS_CHILD | WS_POPUP)) == WS_CHILD)
             send_message( winpos->hwnd, WM_CHILDACTIVATE, 0, 0 );
         else if (!(style & WS_MINIMIZE))
-            set_foreground_window( winpos->hwnd, FALSE, FALSE );
+        {
+            BOOL ok;
+
+            /* NEUTRON noactivate-keepfg (input.c): a WS_EX_NOACTIVATE top-level is activated for its own
+             * thread only, the foreground stays with the other thread that holds it */
+            if (!neutron_noactivate_keepfg( winpos->hwnd, "SetWindowPos", &ok ))
+                set_foreground_window( winpos->hwnd, FALSE, FALSE );
+        }
     }
 
     if(!(orig_flags & SWP_DEFERERASE))
--- a/dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h
+++ b/dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h
@@ -107,6 +107,7 @@
 extern HWND get_active_window(void);
 extern HWND get_capture(void);
 extern BOOL neutron_noactivate_click( HWND top );
+extern BOOL neutron_noactivate_keepfg( HWND top, const char *caller, BOOL *ok );
 extern HWND get_focus(void);
 extern DWORD get_input_state(void);
 extern DWORD get_last_input_time(void);
